{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/921632-accessing-the-lair","id":921632,"title":"Accessing the Lair","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T12:43:05-07:00","id":921632,"title":"Accessing the Lair","content":"So, I wanted to check a few things on a Beast entering their Lair, I know the rules in the book though I figured I'd make a topic here so I can check my understanding, as I have a habit of skim-reading or making assumptions.<br /> <br /> My main question is to check if the only ways to gain access to the Lair is through Primordial Pathways (which overlays the Lair over the Beast's current location), Skeleton Key (accessing it through a gateway to an otherworld) or via a mortal's dreams using Under the Bed?<br /> <br /> I suppose one could also gain access to the Lair by creating a new Chamber out of their current location, though are those things mentioned above all the only ways to access the Lair (outside of doing the ol' mind-meld with the Horror in the Lair, seeing through it's eyes whilst the Beast is still outside)?<br /> <br /> Also, for quick reference, do all of these make the Beast fuse and become their Horror form or can they still remain in human form seperate from the Horror in some cases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:57:13-07:00","id":921639,"title":"","content":"If I'm correct you can also 'Commune' with the beast, spend time concentrating and take control of the beast in the lair. You remain in the physical world (and lose defense) but it's useful if your beast needs to do something that you don't necessarily need to be there for (such as finding a book in a library you have in one of your chambers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:16:04-07:00","id":921652,"title":"","content":"The only time you can enter the Lair and not merge with the Horror is when it has the Slumbering condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:22:58-07:00","id":921654,"title":"","content":"Interesting that outside of the communing (I tried describing that in my OP ^^<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that each way of entering the Lair needs a roll, so it's actually very possible to fail opening a Pathway or otherwise slipping into the Dream from elsewhere. Primordial Pathways seems particularly tough to achieve consistently, though I do know there are modifiers to it, including the Satiety Conditions a Beast can achieve.<br /> <br /> This is a bit concerning if someone manages to attack the Heart of the Lair... Though I expect the Horror itself could take care of it if the Beast is somehow too weak or otherwise unable to find a way into the Lair conveniently...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:00:22-07:00","id":921707,"title":"","content":"Considering how much health the Heart has and the long interval between rolls, that's almost never going to be what kills a Beast. Far more likely that the Horror or the mortal self will die first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:09:09-07:00","id":921710,"title":"","content":"I've wondered if the horror is in one chamber all the way across the lair, and you enter the lair in a different lair,does the horror slingshot to you for the merge? <br /> <br /> Secondly a question about merging, it states the horror can't use nightmares, and may use low satiety effects on ativisms, even when not low, but when you merge you can not use the low level satiety effects unless you're low. But it doesn't say if you can use nightmares or not when merged","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}